                <div class="card shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4">
                    <h4 class="mb-3">Overview</h4>
                    <p>
                        This interface allows you to create entries for <strong>CONSIGNEE</strong>, 
                        <strong>PACKAGE</strong>, <strong>PREALERT</strong>, and <strong>COURIER</strong> sync types.
                    </p>
                    
                    <div class="info-box">
                        <strong><i class="bi bi-info-circle-fill"></i> New: PREALERT Webhooks</strong><br>
                        PreAlert webhooks allow you to receive automatic updates when new pre-alerts are created, matched with existing packages, or synced with the warehouse system. 
                        This is ideal for tracking incoming shipments and managing customs clearance processes.
                    </div>

                    <h3>CONSIGNEE Sync</h3>
                    <p>
                        <strong>CONSIGNEE</strong> pulls data from your system into the warehouse. Required fields are:
                        <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>, and <code>mailbox</code>. 
                        <br>
                        The following fields are optional: <code>branch</code> and <code>email</code>.
                    </p>
                    <p>An array of objects is required. Active false will result in deletion.</p>
                    <pre>[
  {
    "first_name": "John",
    "last_name": "Doe",
    "mailbox": "OZ122",
    "branch": "KN(optional)",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com(optional)",
    "active": true
  },
  {
    "first_name": "John 2",
    "last_name": "Doe 2",
    "mailbox": "OZ123",
    "branch": "CL",
    "email": "john2.doe2@example.com",
    "active": true
  }
]</pre>

                    <h3>PREALERT Sync <span class="badge badge-matched">NEW</span></h3>
                    <p>
                        <strong>PREALERT</strong> pushes pre-alert data to your system when new shipments are expected. 
                        This includes tracking information, package details, and match scores with existing inventory.
                    </p>
                    <p><strong>PreAlert Data Structure:</strong></p>
                    <pre>{
  "prealerts": [
    {
      "uuid": "encrypted_unique_id",
      "tracking_no": "TRK123456789",
      "merchant": "Amazon",
      "shipper": "John Doe",
      "consignee": "Jane Smith",
      "description": "Electronics and accessories",
      "weight": 2.5,
      "dimensions": "30x20x10",
      "value": 150.00,
      "package_type": "box",
      "destination": "Kingston, Jamaica",
      "expected_arrival": "2024-03-15T00:00:00.000Z",
      "status": "pending",
      "match_score": 85,
      "match_level": "high",
      "matched_package_id": "optional_matched_package_uuid",
      "matched_at": "2024-03-10T12:00:00.000Z",
      "courier_code": "RM",
      "courier_id": "encrypted_courier_id",
      "company_id": "encrypted_company_id",
      "created_at": "2024-03-01T10:00:00.000Z",
      "updated_at": "2024-03-10T12:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}</pre>

                    <p><strong>PreAlert Status Values:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><span class="badge badge-pending">pending</span> - PreAlert created but not yet processed</li>
                        <li><span class="badge badge-matched">matched</span> - Matched with existing package in warehouse</li>
                        <li><span class="badge badge-synced">synced</span> - Successfully synced with warehouse system</li>
                        <li><span class="badge badge-pending">failed</span> - Sync failed, requires attention</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p><strong>Match Levels:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>high</strong> (80-100%) - Strong match, likely same package</li>
                        <li><strong>medium</strong> (50-79%) - Possible match, requires review</li>
                        <li><strong>low</strong> (0-49%) - Weak match, likely different package</li>
                    </ul>

